h him the  legacy of a movement that touched  America's conscious and changed his  history at the forefront of the major  civil rights events of our time from the  Montgomery bus boycott to protest  against apartheid he has served as a  tireless beacon for non-violence and  social justice as a pastor and civil  rights advocate he co-founded the  Southern Christian Leadership Conference  and championed the cause of peace and  freedom around the world the United  States proudly honors this outstanding  leader  Joseph's medicine crow as a warrior and  living legend history flows through dr.  Joseph medicine crow hi bird born on a  reservation and raised by traditional  grandparents he became the first member  of his tribe to earn a master's degree  for his valiant service in World War two  he was awarded the status of crow war  chief and his renowned studies of the  first Americans and contributions to  cultural and historical preservation  have been critical to our understanding  of America's history Joe medicine crow  is a symbol of strength and survival and  the United States honors him for his  dedication to this country and to all  Native Americans  Stuart milk accepting on behalf of his  uncle Harvey Bernard milk  Harvey Bernard milk dedicated his life  to shattering boundaries and challenging  assumptions as one of the first openly  gay elected officials in this country  he changed the landscape of opportunity  for the nation's gay community  throughout his life he bought  discrimination with visionary courage  and conviction before his tragic death  in 1978 he wisely noted hope will never  be silent and called upon Americans to  stay true to the guiding principles of  equality and justice for all  Harvey Milk's voice will forever echo in  the hearts of all do to carry forward  his timeless message  Sandra Day O'Connor  Sandra Day O'Connor has paved the way  for millions of women to achieve their  dreams completing law school in just two  years he graduated thir